{"nodes": [{"id": "concepts_how_it_works_store_recover_lifecycle", "label": "Store / Recover Lifecycle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "## Store / Recover Lifecycle", "rationale": "Failover sits between a Spring bean and its upstream dependency: on success it saves the result, on failure it serves the last saved result. This keeps recovery transparent so calling code never changes.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_entry_lifecycle_states", "label": "Entry Lifecycle States (Live / Stale / Expired)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "## Entry Lifecycle States", "rationale": "Callers receive upToDate=true in Live and upToDate=false in Stale; expired entries are never served so a caller can never silently act on data past its TTL.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_handler_chain", "label": "Handler Chain (decorator, built inside-out / invoked outside-in)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "## Handler Chain and Execution Order", "rationale": "Three handlers compose as decorators so each concern (metrics, slicing, core store/recover) is independently replaceable via @ConditionalOnMissingBean. The chain is assembled once at startup inside-out and invoked outside-in, making the runtime path the exact reverse of the bean build order. delegateT and delegateR are the same DefaultFailoverHandler instance so composite and per-slice paths share one inner handler and clean() runs once, not twice.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_failoveraspect", "label": "FailoverAspect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### FailoverAspect", "rationale": "A Spring AOP @Around advice resolves the reflected Method and hands control to FailoverExecution. Only Exception triggers recovery; java.lang.Error is rethrown unwrapped because recovery itself allocates and must never run on a dying JVM.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_failoverexecution", "label": "FailoverExecution (Basic | Resilience)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Auto-configuration cross-check", "rationale": "ResilienceFailoverExecution extends BasicFailoverExecution and only wraps the upstream supplier in a circuit breaker, so the recover path and handler order are identical for both execution types.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_advancedfailoverhandler", "label": "AdvancedFailoverHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Recover path (upstream threw)", "rationale": "Outermost layer: times the call, catches recover-path errors so they never break the caller, publishes metrics, then runs RecoveredPayloadHandler. The is-recovered flag is captured BEFORE RecoveredPayloadHandler so it reflects the true store hit/miss rather than the substituted fallback.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_scattergatherfailoverhandler", "label": "ScatterGatherFailoverHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Store path (upstream succeeded)", "rationale": "Middle layer: splits the composite into per-entity slices when payloadSplitter is set, otherwise a transparent pass-through, so the scatter concern costs nothing when unused.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_defaultfailoverhandler", "label": "DefaultFailoverHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### DefaultFailoverHandler", "rationale": "Innermost core: store generates the key, computes expireOn and enriches; recover looks up, checks expiry, enriches and deletes expired entries; clean purges by expiry.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_referentialpayload", "label": "ReferentialPayload envelope", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### ReferentialPayload", "rationale": "A single envelope (name, key, upToDate, asOf, expireOn, payload) wraps every stored entry so metadata travels with the data through every store backend.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_defensive_copy_contract", "label": "Defensive copy contract on FailoverStore.find()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "!!! note Defensive copy contract", "rationale": "find() must return a copy, not a live reference, because callers mutate upToDate and asOf on the returned object; without a copy those mutations would corrupt the persisted entry. See ADR 10.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_referential", "label": "Referential (abstract class)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Referential and ReferentialAware", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_referentialaware", "label": "ReferentialAware (interface)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Referential and ReferentialAware", "rationale": "Interface alternative to the Referential base class for domain types that already have a superclass and cannot inherit.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_store_assembly_chain", "label": "Store Assembly Chain (Async -> MultiTenant -> base)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "## Store Assembly Chain", "rationale": "DefaultFailoverStore (defensive copy) always wraps the raw store; FailoverStoreAsync is added when failover.store.async=true. In multi-tenant mode MultiTenantFailoverStore is outermost and async sits inside it per tenant, because the tenant must be resolved on the calling thread before any executor boundary. See ADR 18 and ADR 54.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_failoverautoconfiguration", "label": "FailoverAutoConfiguration failoverHandler assembly", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Auto-configuration cross-check", "rationale": "Every bean is @ConditionalOnMissingBean so any layer of the chain can be replaced by a user bean without forking the framework.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_expirycleanupscheduler", "label": "ExpiryCleanupScheduler cleanup path", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Cleanup path", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_methodexceptionhandler", "label": "MethodExceptionHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Recover path (upstream threw)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concepts_how_it_works_method_identity_contract", "label": "Method identity threading (@NonNull Method, ADR 52)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Method identity (@NonNull)", "rationale": "The reflected Method is threaded @NonNull through the whole chain down to each scatter slice even though only AdvancedFailoverHandler consumes it (to tag per-method metrics). Threading it uniformly avoids null checks and lets any future decorator tag by method.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "concepts_how_it_works_handler_chain", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_advancedfailoverhandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "## Handler Chain and Execution Order", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_advancedfailoverhandler", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_scattergatherfailoverhandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "build (startup) / invoke (per call)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_scattergatherfailoverhandler", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_defaultfailoverhandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "build (startup) / invoke (per call)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_defaultfailoverhandler", "target": "reference_interfaces_failoverstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### DefaultFailoverHandler", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_failoveraspect", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_failoverexecution", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### FailoverAspect", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_failoverexecution", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_methodexceptionhandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Recover path (upstream threw)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_advancedfailoverhandler", "target": "reference_interfaces_recoveredpayloadhandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Recover path (upstream threw)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_failoverautoconfiguration", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_handler_chain", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Auto-configuration cross-check", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_expirycleanupscheduler", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_defaultfailoverhandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Cleanup path", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_defensive_copy_contract", "target": "reference_interfaces_failoverstore", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "!!! note Defensive copy contract", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_defensive_copy_contract", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_referentialpayload", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### ReferentialPayload", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "reference_interfaces_payloadenricher", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_referential", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Referential and ReferentialAware", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "reference_interfaces_payloadenricher", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_referentialaware", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Referential and ReferentialAware", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_referential", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_referentialaware", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "### Referential and ReferentialAware", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_store_assembly_chain", "target": "configuration_properties_reference_store_async", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "## Store Assembly Chain", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_store_assembly_chain", "target": "reference_interfaces_tenantresolver", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "multi-tenant: async sits inside MultiTenantFailoverStore per tenant", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_store_recover_lifecycle", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_entry_lifecycle_states", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/concepts/how-it-works.md", "source_location": "## Entry Lifecycle States", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "concepts_how_it_works_store_recover_lifecycle", "target": "reference_interfaces_expirypolicy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": 